  "id": "stapedius-muscle",
  "term": "stapedius muscle",
  "definition": "The stapedius muscle is a small middle-ear muscle that can be reached surgically and measured directly to record stapedius reflex activity. In this context, it is used as a biological target for objectively assessing electrically evoked stapedius reflex thresholds, such as during cochlear implantation.",
