      "reasons": [
        "The definition claims that the stapedius muscle is used “to record stapedius reflex activity,” but the packet supports directly measuring electrically evoked stapedius reflex threshold (eSRT) and “electromyographic sensing of the eSRT,” not recording “stapedius reflex activity” in general.",
        "The definition’s framing that the muscle is “a biological target for objectively assessing … stapedius reflex thresholds” is broadly consistent with the packet’s “potential tool for objective eSRT fitting,” but the specific wording about “record … reflex activity” is not supported by the provided text."
